LOGBOOK.md-238-### 1205 — M2 capability truth separates relay reprobe from M3 reconnect (TASK-260715-30lv40)
LOGBOOK.md-239-- DECISION: Full is exactly current authenticated SSH + mandatory packet/TCP + safe DNS + installed/current settings + a fresh validated live relay generation. Degraded preserves the same mandatory base with UDP admission closed and all retired relay associations invalidated. Failed, stopping, reasserting, stale, corrupt, and unknown projections advertise no usable capability bits.
LOGBOOK.md-240-- OWNERSHIP: M2 exclusively owns relay bootstrap/session loss and one bounded relay-only reprobe while the current base stays healthy; it remains publicly connected/degraded and never sets provider reasserting. M3 exclusively owns path, host, route, mandatory/lane-pool, sleep/wake, NAT64, and captive reconnect. A current M3 event cancels M2 timers/attempts before any M3 retry loop begins.
LOGBOOK.md:241:- GENERATION/PRIVACY: Runtime generation remains M1-owned, transport generation is M3-owned, and relay attempt/active generation is M2-owned. Association identity cannot cross that tuple. Schema-2 runtime/capability snapshots add finite reasons, retry owner, generations, and locally validated build/limit evidence while preserving explicit schema-1 responses; remote text and sensitive traffic identifiers remain structurally excluded.
LOGBOOK.md-242-- STOP-LINE GATES: The contract is implementable/testable against injected fakes, but production full/degraded readiness remains false until the accepted M0 composition manifest and a production-authorized DNS runtime policy exist. Current DNS numeric candidates are evidence only. No engine, MTU, lane/window, timing, or overlap value was selected here.
LOGBOOK.md-243-- ANOMALY/HANDOFF: Current M1 code uses one global schema-version equality check and does not yet force every non-usable lifecycle projection to all-false capabilities. Existing `TASK-260715-3edgwz` already owns the required kind-specific schema ranges and truthful M2 projection, so no duplicate task was created.
