LOGBOOK.md-279-### 0736 — TCP admission is atomic, bounded, and destination-free (TASK-260715-zfg9ap)
LOGBOOK.md:280:- DECISION: `TCPAdmissionRegistry` is one generation-scoped mutex authority for pending handshakes, authenticated flows, concurrent channel opens, owned channels, fixed directional queue capacity, live buffered bytes, and phase counts. All ceilings and the measured-safe/HEV evidence gates are caller-injected; denial is synchronous, retains no waiter, maps to SOCKS5 `REP=01`, and explicitly prohibits an SSH open. Reservation identifiers are monotonically allocated without reuse and fail closed with finite `identifier_capacity` pressure before `UInt64` wrap.
LOGBOOK.md-281-- OWNERSHIP: Handshake, flow, and opening tokens provide once-only release plus deinit rollback. Flow termination atomically releases an in-flight open, owned channel, reserved/live bytes, and phase slot before publishing one finite terminal reason. A late open completion after terminal cleanup is counted as a discarded event rather than a second release. Existing admitted flows continue byte/buffer progress while new work is rejected under pressure.
LOGBOOK.md-282-- DIAGNOSTICS: Runtime schema v1 is additively extended to 139 fixed counters, 75 fixed gauges, and two 12-bucket cumulative histograms. Registry-owned current gauges publish through a generation-scoped fixed-size atomic coalescer and reconcile into snapshots independently of the bounded event lane, so dropped counter/histogram ingestion remains observable without leaving phantom flow/open/channel/byte gauges. The TCP surface contains only aggregate pressure/terminal tokens, counts, bytes, health, and channel-open latency; it accepts no destination, hostname, address, port, payload, credential, flow/channel ID, or free-form label. Maximum populated encoding is 13,568 bytes of the 65,536-byte limit and generation advancement isolates stale publications.
LOGBOOK.md-283-- VERIFICATION: Eighteen admission tests cover below/at/above every independent ceiling, 128/256-way reserve races, 500 release/open and 500 late-callback races, 250 explicit-release/deinit ownership races, ID exhaustion, queued-byte overflow, session-health races, 8,000 sustained pressure rejects alongside 2,000 admitted-flow progress steps, every terminal reason across 320 churn lifecycles, and exact local/exported baseline recovery. The bounded-queue convergence probe passes 20/20 runs; focused normal and TSan admission/diagnostics suites pass; `make validate-core` passes boundary/native gates, 306 tests in 27 suites, and the post-test build; strict recursive Swift format, privacy/boundary, diff, and board validation pass.
--
LOGBOOK.md-297-- DECISION: The shared iOS/macOS HEV boundary remains IPv4 loopback plus a fresh per-generation RFC 1929 capability; loopback/TCP peer metadata is explicitly not process identity. A descriptor reaches `SSHProxyAdapter` only after capability proof and is positioned at the first CONNECT-request byte.
LOGBOOK.md-298-- CORRECTION: Current `HEVSOCKSBoundary` uses `SO_RCVTIMEO`, which is a per-receive inactivity bound and can restart as bytes arrive; authentication sends have no deadline. The pending set is count-bounded, but current source does not prove an absolute accept-to-auth deadline. M1 must compute one monotonic deadline at accept, apply its remaining budget across greeting/auth reads, comparisons, and replies without progress extension, and prove slow-trickle/reply-stall eviction plus slot/descriptor release on iOS and macOS.
LOGBOOK.md-299-- CONTRACT: IPv4, IPv6, and strict ASCII/IDNA domain CONNECT requests map once to the accepted candidate-neutral `SSHTransport.openDirectTCPIP` seam, using the verbatim remote-resolved destination, constant sanitized `127.0.0.1:0` originator, caller-injected `SSHChannelPolicy`, and no retry, lane migration, or optimistic success. Each direction owns one bounded buffer; EOF halves remain independent; first-terminal-claim cleanup releases socket, channel, tasks, timers, and reservations once.
LOGBOOK.md:300:- RESOURCE: Adapter capacity is an atomic non-waiting reservation bounded by the HEV session ceiling and the measured M0/SSH/Core memory equation; exact flow, chunk, queue, window, and timeout values remain injected measurement inputs for M1/M3 rather than promoted constants. Diagnostics are aggregate schema-v1 only and exclude credentials, SOCKS bytes, endpoints, hostnames, payloads, and flow identifiers.
LOGBOOK.md-301-- TRACEABILITY: The accepted-input resource names nonexistent `TASK-260715-100wu6`; the accepted SSH seam is `TASK-260720-100wu6`. This is recorded as an input-ID typo only, with no SSH engine/observability decision reopened.
