LOGBOOK.md-339-### 0351 — Owned VPN preferences are shared policy with thin platform clients (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
LOGBOOK.md-340-- DECISION: `ReluxTunnelCore` owns the serialized exact-predicate repository, immutable canonical configuration, 15-second callback tokens, stable errors, one-stale retry, and reload verification. The iOS/macOS adapter modules only translate public `NetworkExtension` objects and notifications into the injectable core seams.
LOGBOOK.md-341-- SAFETY: Ensure never enables; the explicit enable result names the OS-level possibility that another enterprise VPN is disabled. Duplicate repair removes every freshly revalidated current-schema inactive exact-owned manager, reloads after each removal, proves zero, then recreates one. Unmarked, unrelated, wrong-type, corrupt duplicate, active duplicate, and future-owned managers are zero-write paths.
LOGBOOK.md:342:- IDENTITY: The complete host/provider/App Group/Keychain `PlatformVPNIdentity` remains injectable for deterministic fixtures. Both production factories fail closed until `TASK-260715-ypo7yo` supplies accepted signed bindings; no guessed identifier landed.
LOGBOOK.md-343-- VERIFICATION: 18 deterministic Swift Testing cases cover mixed managers, type confusion, least-data/secret exclusion, idempotency, explicit enable/disable/remove, duplicate repair, future preservation, stale replacement, authorization, save/reload failure, timeout/cancellation late callbacks, and stop timeout. `make validate-core` passes 236 tests in 24 suites plus build; strict format lint and iOS Simulator/macOS Xcode builds pass.
LOGBOOK.md-344-
LOGBOOK.md-345-### 0320 — Provider routing and cleanup share one bounded generation owner (TASK-260715-1bp6eu)
LOGBOOK.md-346-- DECISION: Both platform roots expose identical callback seams and delegate to one core actor. V1 accepts only the four read-only commands, requires a request UUID at the provider boundary, keeps at most 256 active and 256 recently completed request IDs, and retires pending once-only reply gates on stop so a late source callback cannot reach another generation.
LOGBOOK.md-347-- CLEANUP: Every generation receives a fixed 64-handle cleanup registry. Stop immediately rejects work and fans out cancellation, then joins one reverse runtime stop behind an injected ten-second budget. Expiry force-closes registered controllable handles and records only the raw Apple reason, one fixed counter/gauge, and the finite `cleanup_deadline_exceeded` token. Provider fatal failure emits one stable 1001–1009 NSError and the later system stop joins the same cleanup.
LOGBOOK.md-348-- ORDERING: Stop during factory/runtime startup wins, retires late-created handles, and completes the pending Apple start gate before each stop gate. The 60-second startup race and cleanup race use injected clocks and continuations; no correctness sleep or unbounded task-group join is used.
LOGBOOK.md:349:- SCHEMA: Provider stop metadata extends diagnostics v1 to 97 counters, 57 gauges, and 11 finite error codes across the same 10 domains. The schema still retains no endpoints, DNS names, traffic identifiers, secrets, configuration, localized errors, or free-form labels.
LOGBOOK.md-350-- COVERAGE: Shared tests run through iOS and macOS seams for all four commands, hostile/oversized/future/mutating inputs, duplicates, nil handlers, retirement, all raw Apple reasons, startup and cleanup deadlines, stop-wins-start, fatal handoff, deallocation, and two 100-cycle baselines. Existing coordinator tests retain every startup acquisition/cancellation point and route-clear uncertainty coverage.
LOGBOOK.md-351-
LOGBOOK.md-352-### 0245 — VPN lifecycle separates ownership, enablement, system state, and runtime capability (TASK-260715-1q4qhw)
LOGBOOK.md-353-- DECISION: A manager is owned only when its protocol is `NETunnelProviderProtocol`, its provider bundle ID exactly matches the accepted platform binding, and its stable provider-configuration marker matches. Labels, server address, enabled state, profile UUID, schema version, and array order never establish ownership. Every write/remove rechecks a freshly loaded object; unmarked lookalikes and duplicates are zero-write conflicts outside explicit inactive duplicate repair.
LOGBOOK.md-354-- PLATFORM FINDING: Apple limits `loadAllFromPreferences` to configurations created by the calling app, but enabling an enterprise VPN can cause the OS to disable another app's enterprise VPN. Therefore ordinary ensure preserves/creates a disabled configuration and explicit foreground user intent owns enable/save/reload. Relux never mutates the unrelated manager object and reports the system-level enable effect truthfully.
LOGBOOK.md-355-- AUTHORITY: `NETunnelProviderSession.status` is the sole system-session authority; a fresh generation/sequence provider snapshot is the sole runtime capability authority. Host suspension/termination removes observers only. Provider start/stop once-gates and exact deadlines remain extension-owned and join the accepted coordinator cleanup.
LOGBOOK.md:356:- RESIDUAL: Exact four-target bundle IDs, App Group, Keychain group, and entitlements are not yet accepted (`TASK-260715-ypo7yo`). Shared implementation proceeds through injected identities, while production composition fails closed instead of inventing values. Human ratification stays decoupled in `TASK-260717-1dsqnj`.
LOGBOOK.md-357-
LOGBOOK.md-358-### 0211 — Coordinator fault suite freezes ownership boundaries and resource baselines (TASK-260715-32virr)
LOGBOOK.md-359-- DECISION: Fault injection uses the coordinator's injected cancellation-check seam to fail at fourteen exact before/after ownership boundaries. This keeps production code unchanged while proving reverse rollback, one disconnecting publication, one terminal publication, exact error mapping, and single cleanup for configuration, SSH, TCP, DNS, packet plane, settings, and packet-read ownership.
