Verdict: **changes requested**. `TASK-260715-ypo7yo — Define the Apple identifier and entitlement matrix` is routed to `analysis`; it was not left in `reviewing`.

Key blockers:

- C1 Mac Development profiles incorrectly use `packet-tunnel-provider-systemextension`. Development signing requires `packet-tunnel-provider`; the suffix is for direct Developer ID distribution. [Apple guidance](https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/800887)
- The matrix conflates registered `group.*` App Groups with distinct Team-ID-prefixed macOS identifiers. New macOS projects should use the provisioned `group.*` style. [Apple guidance](https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/721701)
- Entitlement assertion A10 omits signing-generated entitlements, so it would reject valid signed bundles.
- App Sandbox rationale incorrectly attributes host sandboxing to Apple rather than the project’s Sparkle architecture.

Gate results:

- Producer validator: exit 0
- Reviewer signing-channel gate: exit 1
- Legacy preservation guard: exit 0
- Board validation: exit 0

Full evidence: [reviewer verdict](/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel/.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_reviewer-verdict-01.md). Parent aggregation moved the story to `analysis` and epic to `to-dev`.
